{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/dropreports"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"A report of each drop, in the order they happen, from recovery onwards.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"title":"dropReports","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dropReports","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncQueue","preciseIdentifier":"s:11AsyncQueues0A5QueueV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"DropReport","preciseIdentifier":"s:11Persistence10DropReportO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"Persistence"}],"externalID":"s:11Persistence12SegmentStoreV11dropReports11AsyncQueues0F5QueueVyAA10DropReportOGvp","remoteSource":{"fileName":"SegmentStore.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Persistence\/SegmentStore.swift#L163"}},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"dropReports"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues\/AsyncQueue","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"AsyncQueue","preciseIdentifier":"s:11AsyncQueues0A5QueueV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"DropReport","preciseIdentifier":"s:11Persistence10DropReportO"},{"kind":"text","text":"> { "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"kind":"text","text":" }"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reports wait, without a bound, until they are read, so none is missed by reading late."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Drops are rare (each is a whole segment, or bytes recovery couldn’t read), so they don’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pile up. The sequence ends once the store is gone and every report has been read."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One task reads the reports at a time. The first iterator to read holds them until its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iteration ends or it is released; a second reader meanwhile waits its turn, logging a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"warning once, then reads on from the next report, so the first gets every report in order."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A reader cancelled while it waits returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"references":{"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport":{"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DropReport"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DropReport"}],"title":"DropReport","abstract":[{"text":"Records a store dropped before they were delivered, and why.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore":{"type":"topic","title":"SegmentStore","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" that keeps records in a directory of append-only segment files, bounded in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"size, until they are delivered."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}]},"doc://AsyncQueues/documentation/AsyncQueues/AsyncQueue":{"title":"AsyncQueue","identifier":"doc:\/\/AsyncQueues\/documentation\/AsyncQueues\/AsyncQueue","url":"\/documentation\/asyncqueues\/asyncqueue","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncQueue","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AsyncQueue","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Elements in the order they are enqueued, kept until they are read; one reader at a time reads"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them."}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/RecordStore":{"type":"topic","title":"RecordStore","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RecordStore"}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/recordstore","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where a tracker keeps each record until it is delivered, so records survive the app ending."}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RecordStore"}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/dropReports":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/dropreports","kind":"symbol","title":"dropReports","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","abstract":[{"text":"A report of each drop, in the order they happen, from recovery onwards.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dropReports","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncQueue","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11AsyncQueues0A5QueueV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"DropReport","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11Persistence10DropReportO"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence":{"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/persistence","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","title":"Persistence","abstract":[{"text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so the records a tracker tracked survive the app ending.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol"}}}